      "config_help_batt_discharge_entity": "number-enheten SEM skriver til for å begrense batteriutlading (f.eks. inverterens maks. utladingseffekt).",
      "config_help_batt_max_discharge": "Det harde taket for ALL batteriutlading (hus + EV sammen) — skrives til inverterens utladingsgrense. EV assist-grensen ovenfor er en delgrense av denne.",
      "config_help_batt_protection": "Begrenser batteriutlading til maks.-effekten over for å beskytte det og beholde en reserve.",
      "config_help_battery_arbitrage": "Når den dynamiske eksportprisen er høy nok til å slå kostnaden ved å lade opp igjen senere, utlades batteriet til nettet for å selge lagret energi. Valgfritt; utlader aldri under reserve-SOC.",
      "config_help_battery_bidirectional": "Enable if this battery's discharge-power entity is a bidirectional setpoint — one number entity for both charge and discharge, e.g. a Sessy. SEM then charges by writing a negative value to it. Leave off for a one-way forcible-discharge entity (e.g. Huawei).",
      "config_help_battery_cycles_sensor": "A hardware lifetime battery-cycle counter (e.g. from your Sonnen/Huawei integration). When set, SEM shows this instead of its throughput estimate. Autodetected on the battery device first.",
      "config_help_battery_power_sensor": "Live battery power (W, negative = discharge). Set this if battery power reads 0 while your Energy Dashboard has only battery energy. Autodetected first.",
      "config_help_battery_soc_sensor": "Sensoren SEM leser for batteriets ladenivå (%). Angi denne hvis SEM ikke oppdaget den automatisk — SOC er i Energi-dashbordet, men vises som utilgjengelig.",
      "config_help_bs_block_mode": "Pick the cheapest contiguous price window instead of scattered cheapest slots — slightly higher cost, less inverter start/stop cycling.",
      "config_help_bs_capacity": "Usable battery capacity in kWh — used to size pre-charge targets.",
      "config_help_bs_cycle_cost": "How much one stored kWh costs in battery wear. Set to 0 if you don't want SEM to penalise cycles.",
